From: transentient <cliff.judge@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 13:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8250: tag the CPU interconnect paths ACTIVE_ONLY

The CPU nodes' bandwidth paths to DDR carry no tag, which the RPMh
interconnect driver treats as QCOM_ICC_TAG_ALWAYS: the last bandwidth the
cpufreq governor voted stays in the AMC, WAKE and SLEEP buckets alike, so
the BCM voter never programs a sleep value and the CPUs' DDR vote (SH0,
SH4, MC0, ACV) stands through suspend-to-idle.  Measured on the Retroid
Pocket 5: the RSC sleep TCS holds a single entry (MM0 off), DDR never
enters self-refresh and the SoC never reaches cxsd/aosd (qcom_stats 0).
sm8550 and sm8650 tag the same paths QCOM_ICC_TAG_ACTIVE_ONLY; do the
same here so the sleep bucket drops to zero when the APSS sleeps.
